<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<!--
	The background of Widget.OverlapPopupMenu, and the same rounded rectangle Material's
	popup_background_material draws — except held 12dp clear of the bottom of the popup window, so
	the window has room inside itself for the elevation shadow.

	A PopupWindow reserves shadow room by growing its surface ceil(2 * z) on every side, which is a
	constant, but the shadow it has to hold is not: the spot light sits at the top edge of the display
	(light_y = 0dp, light_z = 500dp, light_radius = 800dp), so a popup opened low on the screen throws
	its shadow that much further down — around 13dp of offset plus a 13dp penumbra at 8dp of elevation
	near the bottom of a phone, against the 16dp the surface reserved. The shadow was cut off along a
	hard horizontal line, and only looked right when the drawer was scrolled far enough for the popup
	to open near the top of the screen.

	The inset is empty space, not padding the user sees: the popup lays its content out inside the
	background's padding, so the rounded rectangle still ends exactly where the last row does.

	ThemeEngine's popup hook re-fills this with the theme card colour at the user's corner radius,
	carrying the inset over — the colour and radius here only apply if that hook does not run.
-->

<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
	android:insetBottom="12dp">

	<shape android:shape="rectangle">

		<corners android:radius="2dp" />
		<solid android:color="?android:attr/colorBackground" />

	</shape>

</inset>
